        },
        {
          "sentence_id": "sentence_1d25d4d0be5e18e8ef2b",
          "document_start": 751,
          "document_end": 771,
          "text": "2.7 Fluid Mechanics;",
          "section_id": "section_2c8bfa6b6a02",
          "start": 751,
          "end": 771,
          "chunk_start": 751,
          "chunk_end": 771,
          "sentence_document_start": 751,
          "sentence_document_end": 771,
          "sentence_complete": true
        },
        {
          "sentence_id": "sentence_9744ee782537c0e98418",
          "document_start": 772,
          "document_end": 804,
          "text": "intervening text may be omitted]",
          "section_id": "section_2c8bfa6b6a02",
          "start": 772,
          "end": 804,
          "chunk_start": 772,
          "chunk_end": 804,
          "sentence_document_start": 772,
          "sentence_document_end": 804,
          "sentence_complete": true
        },
        {
          "sentence_id": "sentence_05864a4a5da7369880f4",
          "document_start": 806,
          "document_end": 910,
          "text": "It is by this very same logic that the stagnation pressure, temperature, and density must also increase.",
          "section_id": "section_2c8bfa6b6a02",
          "start": 806,
          "end": 910,
          "chunk_start": 806,
          "chunk_end": 910,
          "sentence_document_start": 806,
          "sentence_document_end": 910,
          "sentence_complete": true
        },
        {
          "sentence_id": "sentence_3ec46be0bec85138bbee",
          "document_start": 912,
          "document_end": 932,
          "text": "[Source paragraph 4;",
          "section_id": "section_2c8bfa6b6a02",
          "start": 912,
          "end": 932,
          "chunk_start": 912,
          "chunk_end": 932,
          "sentence_document_start": 912,
          "sentence_document_end": 932,
          "sentence_complete": true
        },
        {
          "sentence_id": "sentence_b26b56d589fa42df5a00",
          "document_start": 933,
          "document_end": 953,
          "text": "2.7 Fluid Mechanics;",
          "section_id": "section_2c8bfa6b6a02",
          "start": 933,
          "end": 953,
          "chunk_start": 933,
          "chunk_end": 953,
          "sentence_document_start": 933,
          "sentence_document_end": 953,
          "sentence_complete": true
        },
        {
          "sentence_id": "sentence_aab06791e18bc6ea4fce",
          "document_start": 954,
          "document_end": 986,
          "text": "intervening text may be omitted]",
          "section_id": "section_2c8bfa6b6a02",
          "start": 954,
          "end": 986,
          "chunk_start": 954,
          "chunk_end": 986,
          "sentence_document_start": 954,
          "sentence_document_end": 986,
          "sentence_complete": true
        },
        {
          "sentence_id": "sentence_5dbbadee26feece7888f",
          "document_start": 988,
          "document_end": 1093,
          "text": "We have discussed some governing equations, but let us break for a moment to discuss why a gas shocks up.",
          "section_id": "section_2c8bfa6b6a02",
          "start": 988,
          "end": 1093,
          "chunk_start": 988,
          "chunk_end": 1093,
          "sentence_document_start": 988,
          "sentence_document_end": 1093,
          "sentence_complete": true
        },
        {
          "sentence_id": "sentence_6b7b849a305b689c3498",
          "document_start": 1094,
          "document_end": 1197,
          "text": "If we closely examine Equation 2.170, we see that a higher pressure causes a faster motion of the wave.",
          "section_id": "section_2c8bfa6b6a02",
          "start": 1094,
          "end": 1197,
          "chunk_start": 1094,
          "chunk_end": 1197,
          "sentence_document_start": 1094,
          "sentence_document_end": 1197,
          "sentence_complete": true
        },
        {
          "sentence_id": "sentence_73462e794b623e2f63bf",
          "document_start": 1198,
          "document_end": 1337,
          "text": "If we imagine a shock wave as depicted in Figure 2.27 moving to the right, we can pick out three points that we shall follow for some time.",
          "section_id": "section_2c8bfa6b6a02",
          "start": 1198,
          "end": 1337,
          "chunk_start": 1198,
          "chunk_end": 1337,
          "sentence_document_start": 1198,
          "sentence_document_end": 1337,
          "sentence_complete": true
        },
        {
          "sentence_id": "sentence_56b050243d8f1d6093f9",
          "document_start": 1338,
          "document_end": 1438,
          "text": "Point A is essentially the beginning of the pressure increase and at the unshocked initial pressure.",
          "section_id": "section_2c8bfa6b6a02",
          "start": 1338,
          "end": 1438,
          "chunk_start": 1338,
          "chunk_end": 1438,
          "sentence_document_start": 1338,
          "sentence_document_end": 1438,
          "sentence_complete": true
        },
        {
          "sentence_id": "sentence_cb636a7742954a05b4bb",
          "document_start": 1439,
          "document_end": 1586,
          "text": "Point B is at some pressure in between the peak pressure of the shock and the initial pressure of the material into which the shock is propagating.",
          "section_id": "section_2c8bfa6b6a02",
          "start": 1439,
          "end": 1586,
          "chunk_start": 1439,
          "chunk_end": 1586,
          "sentence_document_start": 1439,
          "sentence_document_end": 1586,
          "sentence_complete": true
        },
        {
          "sentence_id": "sentence_9b9e4ed44c1ee84e4761",
          "document_start": 1587,
          "document_end": 1625,
          "text": "Point C is at the peak shock pressure.",
          "section_id": "section_2c8bfa6b6a02",
          "start": 1587,
          "end": 1625,
          "chunk_start": 1587,
          "chunk_end": 1625,
          "sentence_document_start": 1587,
          "sentence_document_end": 1625,
          "sentence_complete": true
        },
        {
          "sentence_id": "sentence_48377f5b764eac2103ac",
          "document_start": 1626,
          "document_end": 1774,
          "text": "From Equation 2.170, we see that the local velocity of point B must be greater than point A and that the local velocity of point C is greater still.",
          "section_id": "section_2c8bfa6b6a02",
          "start": 1626,
          "end": 1774,
          "chunk_start": 1626,
          "chunk_end": 1774,
          "sentence_document_start": 1626,
          "sentence_document_end": 1774,
          "sentence_complete": true
        },
        {
          "sentence_id": "sentence_6eccb9aa6469c500fca0",
          "document_start": 1775,
          "document_end": 1888,
          "text": "This means that at some time  $t$ , these points must converge, thereby forming a step discontinuity in pressure.",
          "section_id": "section_2c8bfa6b6a02",
          "start": 1775,
          "end": 1888,
          "chunk_start": 1775,
          "chunk_end": 1888,
          "sentence_document_start": 1775,
          "sentence_document_end": 1888,
          "sentence_complete": true
        },
        {
          "sentence_id": "sentence_3176a37dc16c487d718b",
          "document_start": 1889,
          "document_end": 2070,
          "text": "This step discontinuity is the way we model the shock—there is actually a very small distance over which a shock will develop so that the pressure increase is rapid, but continuous.",
          "section_id": "section_2c8bfa6b6a02",
          "start": 1889,
          "end": 2070,
          "chunk_start": 1889,
          "chunk_end": 2070,
          "sentence_document_start": 1889,
          "sentence_document_end": 2070,
          "sentence_complete": true
        },
        {
          "sentence_id": "sentence_940addbb804def8dd056",
          "document_start": 2071,
          "document_end": 2156,
          "text": "With this information, we see that compression shocks are the only admissible shocks.",
          "section_id": "section_2c8bfa6b6a02",
          "start": 2071,
          "end": 2156,
          "chunk_start": 2071,
          "chunk_end": 2156,
          "sentence_document_start": 2071,
          "sentence_document_end": 2156,
          "sentence_complete": true
        },
        {
          "sentence_id": "sentence_9fb3280e6c136e8c79fb",
          "document_start": 2157,
          "document_end": 2226,
          "text": "Later we will introduce rarefactions that are the converse of shocks.",
          "section_id": "section_2c8bfa6b6a02",
          "start": 2157,
          "end": 2226,
          "chunk_start": 2157,
          "chunk_end": 2226,
          "sentence_document_start": 2157,
          "sentence_document_end": 2226,
          "sentence_complete": true
        },
        {
          "sentence_id": "sentence_3fb097c7e9edda4bfe31",
          "document_start": 2227,
          "document_end": 2335,
          "text": "Since the pressure decreases in a rarefaction wave, the wave will tend to spread out over time and distance.",
          "section_id": "section_2c8bfa6b6a02",
          "start": 2227,
          "end": 2335,
          "chunk_start": 2227,
          "chunk_end": 2335,
          "sentence_document_start": 2227,
          "sentence_document_end": 2335,
          "sentence_complete": true
        },
        {
          "sentence_id": "sentence_49044a46b3de81c85711",
          "document_start": 2337,
          "document_end": 2357,
          "text": "[Source paragraph 5;",
          "section_id": "section_2c8bfa6b6a02",
          "start": 2337,
          "end": 2357,
          "chunk_start": 2337,
          "chunk_end": 2357,
          "sentence_document_start": 2337,
          "sentence_document_end": 2357,
          "sentence_complete": true
        },
        {
          "sentence_id": "sentence_4958e30e654a92c7aa61",
          "document_start": 2358,
          "document_end": 2378,
          "text": "2.7 Fluid Mechanics;",
          "section_id": "section_2c8bfa6b6a02",
          "start": 2358,
          "end": 2378,
          "chunk_start": 2358,
          "chunk_end": 2378,
          "sentence_document_start": 2358,
